60,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Meridian's fixed configuration might be too rigid, but their regional service team could provide the accountability we lack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Anchor's approach of having engineers present through the rollout is the only way to ensure it survives our yards.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Tessera is a trap. A ""partner firm"" for migration is exactly how we ended up with the 2018 pay move disaster.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Anchor's on-site presence is helpful, but Meridian's hosted suite might be easier for our stretched staff to maintain.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Corvus is a nightmare waiting to happen. Modular licenses are the perfect vehicle for the ""slow bleed"" I've discovered.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, do you think Anchor's on-site team can handle the governance issues, or just the technical ones?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"They can handle the physical reality. If they are on the floor, they see the old devices and the peak-season chaos.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward Meridian. A hosted suite means they can't just let the system ""age in place"" on our own racks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Misaki,,I'm worried about Anchor's on-premise requirement. Our administrators are retiring; we can't manage servers anymore.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A very astute point, Misaki. Anchor's server costs will be a hidden tax on our future budgets.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"If we want to avoid the ""nobody in charge"" problem, Meridian's regional service team seems like the safest bet.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I still believe the risk of operational failure in the yard outweighs the risk of server maintenance. Anchor is the safest for the floor.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're thinking about today. I'm thinking about five years from now when the system is a dinosaur. Meridian it is.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree with May. We need a system that doesn't rely on a few heroic individuals to keep it running. Meridian is the most sustainable.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Meridian's fixed configuration and hosted model offer the most predictable cost structure. It limits the ""add-on"" creep I fear.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,I feel we have a consensus on stability and accountability. I'll vote for Meridian.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I cannot ignore the yard risks, but I see the logic regarding the admin shortage. I'll stick to my guns for Anchor.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,"Sorry Ryuji, but I'm voting for the one that won't leave us with a digital ruin. Meridian.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"For the sake of the people left in the office and the crews in the depot, I vote Meridian.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic dictates that predictability in cost and maintenance is the priority. My vote goes to Meridian.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
